.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
time
- time a command
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
time command [ args ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Time runs command with the given arguments and, when it finishes,
reports how long it took.  The report is written on the standard error
as
.sp
.ce
.bd
real NmSs
.sp
where the time is the wall clock, in minutes and seconds.  Command is
looked up in ., /bin and /usr/bin, so time cc hello.c works without a
path.
.sp
Only the wall clock is reported.  The v7 original also printed user and
system CPU time from times(2), and that call is implemented, but a
times(&struct) invocation trips a ccc code-generation bug that computes
the address of the struct as zero, so this program does not call it yet.
.sp
Time's own exit status is the command's, or 1 if the command could not
be found or forked.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
